      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When the Great Southern Railroad crossed Sun in 1906, sand and gravel mining surged, drawing people from surrounding areas to build homes and churches.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://tammanyfamily.blogspot.com/2018/08/the-history-of-sun.html",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Sun became an official village on October 8, 1958, though its post office had been operating since 1851.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://tammanyfamily.blogspot.com/2018/08/the-history-of-sun.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The village sits on high ground north of the Bogue Chitto River, a natural spot that attracted early settlers.",
